# Documentation

`README.md` is the user documentation: install, setup (minimal and full config), the CLI, the
Vite plugin, handler merge and a worked example. It exists **twice, identically**: the root copy
is what GitHub shows, `packages/takibi-hono/README.md` is what npm shows. Edit one and copy it
over the other in the same change (`cmp README.md packages/takibi-hono/README.md` is silent when
they match).

- Links are absolute `https://github.com/...` / `https://...` URLs: a relative link breaks on npm.
- A change to the config, the CLI or the Vite plugin updates the matching section — the
  `Full Config` block, `Usage`, `Handler Merge` — in the same change. Keep the `Full Config`
  block a config that actually passes `parseConfig`.
- Every fenced block declares its language (`ts`, `tsp`, `bash`, `yaml`, `json`, `text`).
  Terminal output and directory trees are `text`.
- Write in English, US spelling. Use the canonical spelling of names: TypeScript, JavaScript,
  OpenAPI (never "Open API"), TypeSpec, npm, GitHub, Hono, oxfmt, oxlint.
- No `TODO` in the docs; parked work belongs in the report.

## The agent rules

The agent rules are `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` and nothing else: `project.mdc` is always applied, the
others by their `globs` (or, for `playbooks.mdc`, on request). Keep each rule's `description` and
`globs` accurate — they decide when it is read. A rule states what the repository actually does —
when the code and a rule disagree, fix the one that is wrong in the same change rather than
leaving them apart.
